Q("What is the standard electrode potential E°?",["The tendency of a half-cell to be reduced under standard conditions relative to the standard hydrogen electrode","The equilibrium constant","The Gibbs free energy","The activation energy"],"The tendency of a half-cell to be reduced under standard conditions relative to the standard hydrogen electrode"),
Q("What is colligative property?",["A property depending on the number of solute particles, not their identity (e.g., boiling point elevation, freezing point depression)","A property depending on particle identity","Solubility","Density"],"A property depending on the number of solute particles, not their identity (e.g., boiling point elevation, freezing point depression)"),
Q("What is osmosis?",["The movement of solvent molecules through a semipermeable membrane from lower to higher solute concentration","Diffusion of solute","A type of distillation","Filtration"],"The movement of solvent molecules through a semipermeable membrane from lower to higher solute concentration"),
Q("What is Raoult's Law?",["The vapour pressure of a solution equals the vapour pressure of the pure solvent × mole fraction of solvent","Dalton's Law","Henry's Law","Boyle's Law"],"The vapour pressure of a solution equals the vapour pressure of the pure solvent × mole fraction of solvent"),
Q("What is Henry's Law?",["The solubility of a gas in a liquid is proportional to the partial pressure of the gas above the liquid","Raoult's Law","Dalton's Law","Boyle's Law"],"The solubility of a gas in a liquid is proportional to the partial pressure of the gas above the liquid"),
Q("What is the Henderson-Hasselbalch equation?",["pH = pKa + log([A⁻]/[HA]) — for calculating pH of a buffer solution","The Nernst equation","The Arrhenius equation","The Gibbs equation"],"pH = pKa + log([A⁻]/[HA]) — for calculating pH of a buffer solution"),
